## How to run it

{{ thor_build.runtime_note }}

1. Download this repository and the two Engram shards of the base model (below).
2. Build the Engram row files from those two shards (`ops/s09_engram_rowfile.py build`, then `verify --full`). The row files are about the size of the two shards and must sit on a local NVMe drive: they are read with O_DIRECT for every token.
3. Start the server:

```bash
v41_server --ckpt <this repo> --keepset <this repo>/reap_keepset.json --engram <row-file dir> --host 127.0.0.1 --port 18108
```

It serves an OpenAI-style `/v1/chat/completions` (streaming and tool calls, with the model's own chat encoding) and `/health`.

